Answer: Two ways I see it:

Way #1:

\begin{code}
tr:nth-of-type(1),
tr:nth-of-type(2),
tr:nth-of-type(3),
tr:nth-of-type(4),
...
tr:nth-of-type(7) {
  display: none;
}
\end{code}

And way #2:

\begin{code}
td:nth-of-type(n) + tr:nth-of-type(n) {
  display: none;
}
\end{code}

I think way #2 is more flexible. n meaning any number.

